# PURPOSE: Keep git from converting line endings where the bytes are the record.
# WHAT GOES HERE: Path patterns with -text: the model's verbatim output and the frozen prompts (build guide 4.5); the sweep configs pinned to CRLF (D26).
# FILLED IN AT STEP: W4.3; D26.
# DO NOT: Remove these lines: the SHA-256 of a prompt or a kernel must hold on every checkout (core.autocrlf is true on Windows).
h2/kernels/** -text
h2/prompts/** -text
# The runner identifies a sweep by the SHA-1 of its file bytes (manifest sweep_sha1). Every run so far was made from a
# CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true on the laptop), so every checkout must give those bytes, on any platform.
configs/sweeps/*.yaml text eol=crlf
